.TH K8S\-RIGHTSIZER\-REPORT 1 "2026-09" "k8s-rightsizer-report" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
k8s\-rightsizer\-report \- turn KRR recommendations into reviewable requests and limits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B k8s-rightsizer-report
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
KRR (robusta\-dev/krr) reads Prometheus history and does the sizing maths. This
tool does not size anything: it records every KRR run in a directory meant to be
committed, proposes only the recommendations that have stopped moving, and emits
those as Kustomize strategic\-merge patches, a Helm values diff, or a pull
request.
.PP
A recommendation is proposed only once it has stayed within
.B \-\-tolerance
per cent across
.B \-\-runs
consecutive runs. Anything still moving is reported as
.RB \(lq "not yet \(em flapping" \(rq
together with the range it has been moving over.
.PP
There is no
.BR \-\-apply .
The cluster changes when the pull request merges and the GitOps tooling rolls it
out, not when this runs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-n " NS" ", " \-\-namespace " NS"
Namespace to scan. Passed to krr; filters a
.B \-\-krr\-json
file.
.TP
.BI \-\-krr\-json " FILE"
Read
.B krr simple \-\-formatter json
output from
.IR FILE ,
or from standard input when it is
.BR \- .
Without this, krr is run for you when it is on PATH.
.TP
.BI \-\-krr\-arg " ARG"
Extra argument passed through to krr. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-history\-dir " DIR"
Where runs are recorded (default:
.BR .rightsizer/history ).
Commit it: it is the only state this tool keeps.
.TP
.BI \-\-patch\-dir " DIR"
Where patches are written by
.B \-\-write
and
.B \-\-pr
(default:
.BR .rightsizer/patches ).
.TP
.BI \-\-tolerance " PCT"
A recommendation counts as unchanged within this per cent (default: 15).
.TP
.BI \-\-runs " N"
Consecutive runs within
.B \-\-tolerance
before a recommendation is proposed (default: 3).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-record
Do not store this run in the history.
.TP
.BI \-\-helm\-values " FILE"
Update this chart's values file instead of emitting patches, and print the
change as a unified diff.
.TP
.BI \-\-helm\-key " W[/C]=PATH"
Where a workload's (or container's) resources live in the values file, as a
dotted path. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-write
Write the patches or the values update to disk.
.TP
.B \-\-pr
Commit the change and the run file on a new branch and open a pull request with
the
.BR gh (1)
CLI.
.TP
.BI \-\-branch " NAME"
Branch name for
.B \-\-pr
(default:
.BR rightsizer/<timestamp> ).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine\-readable output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A report was produced.
.TP
.B non-zero
KRR could not be run or read, or the history could not be read.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run krr, record the run, see what has settled:
.PP
.RS
.B k8s-rightsizer-report \-n payments
.RE
.PP
Ingest a saved run, with a stricter rule:
.PP
.RS
.B k8s-rightsizer-report \-\-krr-json krr.json \-\-tolerance 5 \-\-runs 5
.RE
.PP
Open the pull request:
.PP
.RS
.B k8s-rightsizer-report \-n payments \-\-pr
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
